Teleporting at will:  If you have a ring of teleport control and you
		      have either eaten a Leppie or a have ring of
		      teleportation on, ^T will allow you to ACTUALLY
		      CONTROL WHEN YOU TELEPORT!!  Of course, you need
		      the necessary  experience (for cavemen, around level
		      10, it may vary from character to character).  
		      WARNING:  THIS EATS FOOD!!!!! (voraciously, that is)
		      and if you're hungry, forget it, it won't work.

Wands of Wishing:  The key to these things is not to be greedy.  The 
	    	   maximum number of objects one should wish for is
		   3 (ie, 3 <objects> of <mumble>); the maximum blessing
		   is also 3 (ie, +3 <mumble>).  Rings, wands and armor
		   are only available in lots of one, however.  Also,
	    	   don't wish for a wand of wishing.  This "meta-wish"
		   will only net you said wand with -1 charges.
		   (I like wishing for 3 +3  crysknives, myself)

Scrolls of taming:  Yes sports fans, you can tame the wizard of Yendor
		    and his cuddly little pooch. Tame them, grab the amulet
		    and teleport out of Hell with them (tame monsters
                    teleport with you when you jump levels (iff they're
		    next to you)). One scroll will have both of them
		    under you control.

Quick Endings:  teleport to level 0 from where ever and you're out of there.

Hey, be careful out there--Devito


